  "id": "code_completion/templates/14_generic_lambda_parameters",
  "topic": "code_completion",
  "subtopic": "templates",
  "title": "Generic lambda parameters",
  "summary": "An `auto` parameter of a lambda completes the members of the type the lambda is called with",
  "prose": "The call can come after the lambda, or be the algorithm the lambda is\npassed to. A lambda called with several types completes nothing.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#493",
    "clangd#1768"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Point {\n    int x;\n    int y;\n};\n\ntemplate <class It, class F>\nF for_each(It first, It last, F f) {\n    for (; first != last; ++first) {\n        f(*first);\n    }\n    return f;\n}\n\nvoid scale(Point* begin, Point* end) {\n    auto norm = [](auto p) { return p.; };\n    norm(Point{});\n    for_each(begin, end, [](auto& p) { p.; });\n    auto by = [](const auto& l, const auto& r) { return l. < r.x; };\n    by(*begin, *end);\n    auto echo = [](auto value) { return value.; };\n    echo(Point{});\n    echo(1);\n}\n",
